  "highlights": [
    "C, 50\u00b0 incidence, along-wave view: Parent + Cho (2.4\u00d7) changes return by +1.24 dB and apparent look-current by +0.02 cm/s relative to the parent.",
    "C, 50\u00b0 incidence, along-wave view: Parent + Cho (1\u00d7) changes return by +1.22 dB and apparent look-current by +0.02 cm/s relative to the parent.",
    "X, 50\u00b0 incidence, along-wave view: Parent + Cho (2.4\u00d7) changes return by +9.16 dB and apparent look-current by +0.07 cm/s relative to the parent.",
    "X, 50\u00b0 incidence, along-wave view: Parent + Cho (1\u00d7) changes return by +8.98 dB and apparent look-current by +0.06 cm/s relative to the parent.",
    "Ku, 50\u00b0 incidence, along-wave view: Parent + Cho (2.4\u00d7) changes return by +16.65 dB and apparent look-current by -0.71 cm/s relative to the parent.",
    "Ku, 50\u00b0 incidence, along-wave view: Parent + Cho (1\u00d7) changes return by +16.66 dB and apparent look-current by -0.86 cm/s relative to the parent."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Preliminary first-order small-slope approximation (SSA1), with a linear Bragg reference; not weighted-curvature approximation or a full Maxwell solution.",
    "No shadowing, multiple reflection, breaking foam, or unresolved roughness. Peak Cho slopes in these inputs exceed the weak-slope regime; large-event absolute returns need further electromagnetic validation.",
    "Finite 0.32 m \u00d7 0.64 m Hann-illuminated periodic simulation patch. No claim of a statistically representative satellite footprint. No coherent tiling.",
    "Power is a normalized finite-patch roughness return after subtracting flat-reference aperture leakage, not a calibrated ocean wind product.",
    "HH and VV differ by constant dielectric Bragg factors at each look in SSA1; their normalized Doppler spectra therefore coincide by construction.",
    "Doppler width includes the explicitly differentiated 2 s temporal Hann window. RHS derivatives avoid a finite-difference alias assumption, but time-quadrature sensitivity remains reported.",
    "Apparent-current change is the change from parent-only Doppler converted to horizontal look velocity. Actual parent/current histories are identical; this is not a retrieved physical current.",
    "The Cho model is directional and excludes longitudinal-zero modes. Transverse returns are a model experiment, not a complete directional wind sea.",
    "Kinematic centroid attribution is parent surface derivative versus Cho derivative on the same full geometry; it does not classify free versus parent-locked waves.",
    "Seawater dielectric properties are model assumptions; power ratios and frequency moments at a fixed look are independent of the common polarization prefactor.",
    "Halving temporal sample density changes some significant-return powers by more than 10%; these views require finer time quadrature."
  ],
